A||N||7||p-did||Duke cylinder head commonality (?)||||1||
Z||000000||p-did||09-02-2001||01:36 PM||||Hey guys.  A friend of my brothers has an 87 coupe w/ the Iron Duke.  We also have a 91 Olds Cutlass Calais, also with the same engine.  Well, he overheated his and warped the head.  I've been trying to find a replacement Fiero head, but with no such luck.  I was wondering since the Cutlass has the same engine, will the cylinder head work on the Fiero?  Thanks a lot for any help!  Have a good one!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jay Olson<BR>(AKA "fropuff")<BR>'86 GT, smashed rear fascia, fastback clip, right tail lamp assembly||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||09-02-2001||03:13 PM||||<A HREF="http://www.doverheads.com" TARGET=_blank>These guys</A> have a reference catalog that may help.  You may be able to tell by the engine code letter in the VIN.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pilrulz||09-02-2001||06:20 PM||||ihave a duke head, not sure what year, but i could check.<P>                                  pil||||reg||12
Z||000003||theogre||09-02-2001||08:02 PM||||Don't mess with the head if the 91 motor is good. take the whole motor. Time wise it's not that much different. Also the 91 motor is rated 112-114 HP. (The 91 ECM chip may be part of that but I'm fairly sure the motor has some minor changes to it.)<P>While the motor is out, replace the timing gears.<P>The 91 motor appears the same but it definatly has some diferences. No, I don't know what they all are. (Yes, I'm talking about things other than the filter in the oil pan and the counterbalance unit.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||p-did||09-03-2001||12:35 PM||||Well, the car was going to be our enduro-car, but the engine blew on it.  The PO didn't even check the oil in the two years she owned it.  Looks as if I'll just get a Duke cylinder head.  Are all the years the same?  Thanks a lot.<P>Pilrulz: If you checked on it, I'd really appreciate it.  Thanks again!<P>------------------<BR>Jay Olson<BR>(AKA "fropuff")<BR>'86 GT, smashed rear fascia, fastback clip, right tail lamp assembly||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-03-2001||02:00 PM||||I think the 91 head is compatible but there's no way to be 100% sure w/o checking it over. If the motor fried, that head could be damaged or seriously worn. Check it over very well before you install it. At the least I'd put new valve seals on it while it's off.<P>While the motors are appart.... could you measure the diameter of the TBI bore for me? I'm trying to find out if the 91 has a larger TBI bore. That model of TBI is available with bore diameters between 32 and 48mm. If the 91 is larger that could account for some of the HP increase. <P>Since those TBI's are fairly common used this could be a cheap way to pickup a few HP on the 87-88 4 cylinders. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||p-did||09-03-2001||04:21 PM||||Maybe I won't use the Olds cylinder head.  I just want to make sure I get a good one when I spend the time taking the bastard apart.  I will still measure the TBI bore diameter for ya, Ogre.  You've helped me out a lot as it is.  I might as well get the kid a Fiero one.  It's not my money for one thing.  I just don't know why he wants me to look for all this crap for him.  I should take a commission.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks again!<P>BTW: Will all 4-cylinder Fiero heads match up?  All years I mean.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-03-2001||05:01 PM||||No. The entire engine was reworked for 87 and up.<P>you can find the motor in other 87-88 and up GM cars. I've seen them in Grand Am and Olds Cutlass Calais.<P>Look at the VIN codes. R is the 4 cyl you can be pretty sure is an exact match. Vin U should be the same but I can't say for certian what subtle diferences there are. I think your 91 is a Vin U.<P>Since the 91 is already dead, I'd say give it a try. You can't hurt it any more than it already is. Since these are pushrod motors, the worst thing is it doesn't match the 87 or it's worn and burns some oil. <P>Do what I do... take the whole head assembly. Leave the manifolds and T stat house on it. Then all you need are head gasket, a valve cover gasket, a TBI mounting gasket, and maybe an exhaust donut. (Probly need new spring bolts for the exhaust no matter what...) It's a bit heavier but it saves a whole bunch of time. Then flip them over so you can compare the bottom. Compare the 2 old head gaskets as well. There may be some diference in coolant hole size but all others should line up exactly. (The head gasket is used to control coolant flow from the block to head.) <P>I would take off the TBI to make sure the PCV vac port and IAC passage are clear. May as well check EGR passage since the valve cover gasket comes with a new EGR gasket. (At least Felpro does. EGR has to come off to get valve cover.)<P>You should also replace the head bolts. These motors use Torque To Yield bolts and the OE ones are known to be weak.||||reg||1
